; any_model.claims — the questions, kept beside the model in the repo.
;
; These are the three claims and the query from docs/model.md, written as the
; politics.lib claim-form invocations they are meant to be (kernel §6 /
; politics §7), not as the raw (property …)/(query …) datums they expand to.
;
; model.md's claims block shows only (load "politics.lib.writ"), but that library's
; `swing` form references stdlib's `toggle`, so stdlib must load first — we add
; (load "stdlib.writ") here (a spec omission in model.md).

(load "stdlib.writ")
(load "politics.lib.writ")

(conviction-reachable docket)      ; possible — sanity
(accountability docket)            ; live — holds only while both
                                   ;   restored-by moves exist
(no-permanent-emergency gov)       ; live

(query captured (where (b bureau)) (is b.independence captured))
